  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to the critical situation of IDPs and affected local population: strengthening the communities in Eastern and Western regions of Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project combines multisectoral assistance for local and IDPs in the eastern regions (Dnipropetrovsk and Donetsk regions) and support for IDPs in host communities, in particular in places of compact living in the&#xA0;western&#xA0;regions of Ukraine (Lviv, Ivano-Frankivsk, Ternopil regions).ltbrgtA practical solution to respond to the needs of IDPs and the affected population is to provide a wide range of services in crisis centers. These services will include social, psychological, legal assistance, including Child Friendly Spaces (hereinafter CFS) for children living in Collective Sites, monetary assistance in the form of multi-purpose cash grants, small household repairs, and coverage of housing rental costs.ltbrgtFacilitators will also work in crisis centers, who will contribute to the functioning of mechanisms for providing assistance to affected groups at the community level.ltbrgtA significant addition to the crisis response to the needs of beneficiaries will be the provision of decent living conditions for people in Collective Sites by improving sanitary and hygienic conditions (minor repairs, household appliances, hygiene, access to clean water (in some Collective Sites).ltbrgtAs part of the implementation of the project, it is planned that more than&#xA0;21,502&#xA0;beneficiaries will be provided with protection needs and will receive quality services.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
